     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 8,500 mg three times daily (25,500 mg/day) is about 10 times the maximum daily dose. I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be appropriate. It would put the patient at serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis. A single 8,500 mg dose also can't be made from standard tablet strengths (500, 850 or 1,000 mg).\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Typo:** If you meant 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day), I can enter that now. I can also enter a lower starting dose, such as 500 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Intentional dose:** If there's a reason I don't know about, please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy. If they approve it, the order can go through pharmacy-verified channels with their sign-off documented.\n- **Possible overdose or ingestion:** If this relates to a suspected metformin overdose, that needs toxicology or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US). It wouldn't be handled as a scheduled medication order.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
